{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last","id":1390032,"title":"VTM: Why the Masquerade will last.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-19T12:42:08-07:00","id":1390032,"title":"VTM: Why the Masquerade will last.","content":"The Masquerade is strong, really strong. Like so strong your cockhead players couldn't blow it if they sired A US president on live television. A lot of people don't seem to realise this, so I'll explain why. <br /> <br /> Ignoring the possibility of an unprecedented sequence of astonishing interdependent freak occurrences (you may only guess as to what I am refering too) At least until we move into an era of cyberpunk, the masquerade will last. Unless thermal imaging devices become extroadinarily common place, and vampires don't come up with countermeasures (unlikely, but those might not become widespread) The masquerade should last till Gehenna or till the Technocracy finally commits to a pogrom.<br /> <br /> <b>1: Vampires don't need to resort to Dominate to control the top of society. </b><br /> Vampires are charismatic, Vampires are rich, Vampires can offer illicit pleasures. Vampires can be the best friend of any senator, mayor, police chief, media tycoon, union boss or otherwise anyone worth influencing. <br /> Consider this; Why is the USA always at war? Because the people who make bombs and planes pay politicians millions to vote for war and so that the government will spend billions. While the young rabble vampires most players play aren't multi-millionaires, Vampires that live long rarely don't meet a great standard of wealth; At the very least the &quot;poor&quot; neonates can come together and pool considerable sums, to say nothing of Elders. Wealthy vampires or groups continuously put money into politics and make friends in high places in order to shape their environment to suit them; Ensuring that the chosen elite get low taxes, planning permission for that project, that the law looks the other way, and that certain troublesome institutions stay underfunded; A big gap between rich and poor, lack of education, high crime rate and low trust in law enforcement all combine to create safe, easy feeding grounds. Vampires will finance campaigns so that their Yes-men are far more likely to get into offices and do their best to ensure that troublesome opponents don't get power. Beyond all that, vampires can supply expensive gifts, drugs, sex to those they want to be in good with, and they can blackmail should things deteriorate. Only a few of many vampires need to take this approach, the young don't want to acknowledge it, but they're reaping the benefits of elder machinations without lifting a finger. <br /> <br /> <b>2. Nobody important cares</b><br /> Look at the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westminster_paedophile_dossier\" target=\"_blank\">entire investigations can just go missing</a> and be forgotten about or the case of this<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimmy_Savile_sexual_abuse_scandal\" target=\"_blank\"> high profile star</a>. who really wasn't all that good at keeping a secret; a<i>nd Britain is supposed to be a relatively nice country with little corruption</i>. If elites are content to work with and protect pedophiles, why would they go against vampires? Racism? Racism on the level of violence is for the poor. Rich people need to protect the rich and control the working classes; doesn't matter who it is or what they've done. The wealthy can never be at the mercy of the poor. If one elite goes down, his friends get investigated, then their friends are investigated; They can't have that. That's the real world; In the World of Darkness the problems here are only stronger. Going with the Vampire is all carrot, going against the vampire is all stick. The rich might move against the vampires should the masquerade break and public outcry demands it, but until then, people move only for benefits. <br /> <br /> <b>3. Nobody smart is doing anything about it. Only sore losers go after vampires. </b><br /> &quot;Going with the vampire is all carrot, going against the vampire is all stick&quot; <br /> Even if (and you probably are) ignorant of a vampire's true nature, anyone with 2 or more points in intelligence and some degree of life experience will know what's best left alone. Vampires offer a lot of good things. Going against a vampire is suicidal. At the very least you will lose your job, your chance of getting another job and your reputation. You may be visited by the Mob and/or end up in jail. Knowing more and you will put your family at risk, your life at risk. You might one day find yourself holding a gun and shooting your way around the office; and for what? To persecute a single vampire? How much more of them are there? Does anyone else know? Why haven't people already done something about this? <br /> And then it dawns on you; You really, really should just pretend you don't know anything. <br /> Of course, if you've got nothing to lose, or you're an idiot, knock yourself out. But the closer people are to a possition where they can really do some damage to vampires, the more they have to lose. This is why most hunters are yokels and isolated victims that're easy to deal with. <br /> <br /> <b>3.1 </b>Just because I know it's a point of contention. <br /> Hunters aren't free to do as they please. The Society of Leopold work because they're a disconnected bunch of survival cultists who put their bases in the middle of nowhere, aren't likely to cause serious damage because of the disconnect they use to protect themselves. The Arcanum work because they don't actually do anything. Big government is worth discussing: <br /> The heads of large government organizations are publicly known figures. They, like anyone of importance, receive great generosity from vampires. While on a very small scale, some goverment agents may fight vampires, they are doing so against their organization. The more personnel involved, the more funding, sources and material they use, the more likely they're going to be caught. They have absolutely no chance of organizing anything large scale with other goverment agencies due to the fear of being caught and both parties maintaining secrecy from everyone. These people work against vampires out of greivances or because they want a challenge or because they &quot;wanted to do good&quot;; evidently they're not the best of their organizations. Unlike the off-grid crazies of the Society of Leopold, these people are employees that can be held accountable for their actions and they are supervised by people who do not want them to do what they're doing. Since we'd like to believe that those who work in the government are intelligent (those that got in by nepotism aren't likely to swim against the current) hunters will be few, and all of them will come to believe that human ignorance is what protects humanity (or at the very least these agent-hunters can't attempt to expose vampires without exposing themselves) <br /> <br /> <b>4. Humans don't believe, don't want to believe, and have all the excuses in the world. </b><br /> &quot;wow, CGI is getting really good nowadays&quot; &quot;fake footage&quot; &quot;Is this viral marketing?&quot; &quot;Did you steal this story from a manga?&quot; <br /> Imagine you saw a large man get their throat ripped out by the mouth of a much smaller woman. First off; You'd be in shock. How would you explain what you saw to others? No doubt, everyone would doubt you, so how could not doubt yourself? Most people rationalize it as something else at this point. Memories are mutable they say. It was the shock. Definitely the shock. If the large man was personally close to you and you knew him and you're unwilling to let it go, you probably don't even know where to start, and if you do; you're probably going to get a visitor sometime in the near future. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>5. Oh yeah, and vampires have Disciplines. </b><br /> <br /> That should be all I need to write; your imaginations should be abound with sleeper-agent Dominates and the like, but there's more; According to Hermetic understanding (that thing that makes Tremere Thaumaturgy work): Vampire blood magic should keep up with technology. For everything real that exists, magic should exist for it (As above, so below) . Security cameras? Wiretaps? Bugs? Drones? Internet bots? Cookies? Clickbait? So long as it's worth doing someone'll make a ritual for it. V20's <i>Rites of the Blood </i>painted a colourful vision for the future of vampiric sorcery. Sorcery will proliferate, the Tech-Magic arms race has already begun. Anything anti-vampire on the internet will disappear; the poster none the wiser till the knock on the door. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>6. The Camarilla largely uses Masquerade breaches to assert power over neonates. What the Sabbat do is largely fine. </b><br /> Executions to eliminate political rivals, mercy to gain favours, terror to keep neonates obedient. The Masquerade is the perfect 'just cause' for any Prince. Like a well trained dog, humans will quash most potential problems before they become worthy of a master's attention. It's rare that vampires need to react, and even then it's usually just a phone call. The humans at the top will protect their interests. A few vampires that care enough to foster this environment is usually enough to make up for the vampires that don't (You may thank the Ventrue for their <i>Noblesse oblige </i>or the Lasombra for being control freaks)<br /> <br /> <b>7: The World of Darkness is <i>worse</i> than our world, but it doesn't need to be for the Masquerade to work</b>. <br /> <br /> Hope this was useful. Thanks for reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T12:44:46-07:00","id":1390034,"title":"","content":"<b>3. Nobody smart is doing anything about it. Only sore losers go after vampires. </b><br /> <br /> Except:<br /> <br /> * The NSA<br /> * The FBI<br /> * The Arcanum<br /> * The CDC depending on edition<br /> <br /> And if you are a World of Darkness<br /> <br /> * Werewolves<br /> * Mages<br /> <br /> Seriously, you really don't seem to want organized vampire hunter groups [some with lots of resources] to exist in your game, do you? That's cool but it's headcanon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T13:01:56-07:00","id":1390041,"title":"","content":"Beware the incoming generic wishy washy answer of bland neutrality but questions like this really are ultimately dependent on the storyteller, table, writer, and needs of the chronicle and story. Sure there's a baseline of the setting that we use to provide some guidance, but ultimately, built into the foundation of the system with the Golden Rule, it's very much a 'do as thou will' sorta thing.<br /> <br /> Now that said, I'll also throw in the generic and admittedly kind of smart-ass answer that the Masquerade won't ultimately break because the setting is built upon the conceit that the Masquerade won't break. At the end of the day it's Vampire the Masquerade not Vampire the 'True-Blood-ing' or Vampire the Revealing. Which isn't to say that Broken Masquerade stories and alternate settings aren't fun or interesting, they totally are. Heck the idea of the Masquerade falling and what comes after fascinates me, but I'm also a sucker for Urban Fantasy, Magical Realism, and the like.<br /> <br /> That said, from a baseline perspective, I think the game is best served by having the Masquerade be strong yet fragile. It's kinda like a diamond or certain kinds of metal. It can resist a shocking amount of punishment but if you hit it from the right angle it can still crack.<br /> <br /> In my opinion the Masquerade serves well both for establishing moods and themes and provide easy tension and plot hooks (the classic Masquerade breach that needs to be repaired) but the relative fragility also adds extra layers of nuance.<br /> <br /> How does the vampire relate to their friends and family post-embrace? What can and can't they do because of this social construct? If vampires become too arrogant, humanity could annihilate them like they did in the Inquisition, so they must restrain their natural tendencies towards hubris and condescension.<br /> <br /> Plus, particularly after a long story of vampiric cruelties to both humanity and each other, I find few things are so cathartic as a well prepared gathering of humans coming together and taking back a piece of the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T14:18:30-07:00","id":1390060,"title":"","content":"The paradox is, if the Masquerade is truly impenetrable, what makes the Masquerade necessary at all?<br /> <br /> But I think we already know the Masquerade isn't impenetrable and the vampires aren't invulnerable. If they were, ironically, the Convention of Thorns would never have happened, and the Masquerade never would have been instituted in the first place.<br /> <br /> That said, the way the Camarilla uses the Masquerade to enforce its hegemony is well worth exploring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T14:28:00-07:00","id":1390064,"title":"","content":"I agree. As time has gone by and I've learned more about how corrupt some of the real world powerful institutions are, the more plausible the Masquerade seems. They don't even need to keep a lid on it perfectly. As long as people who claim vampires are real are seen as nuts and videos or whatever that leak are either quashed by the media or &quot;exposed&quot; as fraudulent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T15:27:55-07:00","id":1390076,"title":"","content":"Mortal leadership has always been corrupt and self-interested. Doesn't make them harmless. Not least because humans aren't ultimately rational or predictable in their behavior. History is built of moments of truth in which people didn't do the obvious thing.<br /> <br /> Also, the idea that mortals don't want to believe in the supernatural doesn't work if you know anything about actual humans (unless WoD humans are significantly different from those in the real world), as most people <i>do </i>believe in the supernatural, and real skepticism is relatively rare. It's just that most people's belief in the supernatural is pretty vague and fuzzy in the details. Those who really commit to it are not especially influential, outside of organized religious institutions. But I don't buy that the average person wouldn't <i>love </i>to learn about real vampires.<br /> <br /> But it's true the Masquerade is more resilient than, say, keeping <i>anyone </i>from knowing <i>anything </i>(or keeping any relevant stuff off of Youtube). I rather like the way Requiem formulates it: the Masquerade isn't about keeping people from believing in vampires, it's about keeping people from knowing any specifics about individual vampires and the institutions they belong to. If we're honest, that's how V:tM has always worked in practice, as Kindred have been bending the Traditions to have large mortal support structures, herds, etc., since time immemorial. Yeah, the ones close to you are ghouls, but vampire society takes for granted that a certain portion of humanity knows about them and that this in itself isn't a problem.<br /> <br /> The problem is the <i>wrong </i>people knowing about them, and for anyone not under their thumb to know too many specifics. Better that people remain confused by contradictory entertainment media than know what the Kindred's real weaknesses are. Better that rumors of vampire conspiracies remain vague and misleading than that people know the exact ways they influence the mortal world. Better people have a vague belief that some people might be vampires than that they have a list of names and addresses. If people who shouldn't have this information stumble on it, it's time to do some &quot;cleanup&quot; before it becomes a problem.<br /> <br /> But it <i>can </i>be a problem. In fact, the more the elite elders try to stick their tendrils into mortal institutions, the greater the danger, as humans are just not ever going to be predictable and controllable enough in the long run for the Kindred to ever be as secure as they think they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T15:59:48-07:00","id":1390086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last#post1390032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...your cockhead players couldn't blow it if they sired A US president on live television.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the moment, this isn't saying much.<br /> <br /> A live embrace into vampirism wouldn't even trend on google. It would get lost in the vast, vast sea of of sea-ey vastness of this administration.<br /> <br /> I'm just... too tired to care.<br /> <br /> Hey, maybe that's the best reason the Masqurade won't break. Or, if it did no one would notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T20:28:21-07:00","id":1390167,"title":"","content":"One thing that's always puzzled me: fixable Masquerade breaches are probably inevitable and constant. So when is a Masquerade breach considered something you are presumed to be in the routine process of cleaning up, and when is it something that gets you executed while someone else cleans up your mess as you are dragged to the chopping block? It's a bit like &quot;vulgar without witnessess&quot; in its ambiguity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T20:37:42-07:00","id":1390172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390167#post1390167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that's always puzzled me: fixable Masquerade breaches are probably inevitable and constant. So when is a Masquerade breach considered something you are presumed to be in the routine process of cleaning up, and when is it something that gets you executed while someone else cleans up your mess as you are dragged to the chopping block? It's a bit like &quot;vulgar without witnessess&quot; in its ambiguity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's better than vulgar magick, because that involves some sort of objective truth, which doesn't make sense really. In the case of Masquerade breeches, it comes down to how the authorities, most likely the prince or sheriff locally, decide to treat it. In theory, a prince could decide to kill a vampire in his city for almost anything and a Masquerade breech is just a good excuse. If the prince wants to spare you, then he can make you cover it up or can do so himself and ask for a boon in return. It all comes down to politics - who gains from punishing a Masquerade breech harshly, who gains from leniency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T20:42:24-07:00","id":1390174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390167#post1390167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that's always puzzled me: fixable Masquerade breaches are probably inevitable and constant. So when is a Masquerade breach considered something you are presumed to be in the routine process of cleaning up, and when is it something that gets you executed while someone else cleans up your mess as you are dragged to the chopping block? It's a bit like &quot;vulgar without witnessess&quot; in its ambiguity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends entirely on whose interests a given position favors. Basically, politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25361-sagacious-gamer","name":"Sagacious Gamer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T21:29:24-07:00","id":1390188,"title":"","content":"Well, Gehenna flat out shows a situation where the Masquerade is broken and the world becomes like True Blood.<br /> <br /> So we have the circumstances where it can happen in-canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T23:52:14-07:00","id":1390214,"title":"","content":"Gehenna is Gehenna. I'm discussing business as usual, where fixing a masquerade breach is routine. Not when Lasombra covers the sky and Vicissitude gives all the wildlife their own Zulo Form.<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing I forgot to mention (I posted pretty late)<br /> <br /> Humans <i>want to believe</i> in bullshit. And that's a good thing for the masquerade. People believe in Ghosts, Alien UFOs, Lizard people, The Bemuda triangle, The Illuminati, Satanic cults, fake moonlandings, the world being round... Every one of these things distracts from vampires. You see a vampire attack; Are you sure it's a vampire? If you're invested in lizard people, you'll report lizard people, because confirmation bias is very real.<br /> <br /> And the best bit? The rest of the population can dismiss this stuff as wishful thinking. to finding out that vampires are controlling the government (in exaggerated extremes like &quot;the president is a vampire) is downright <i>juicy</i>. Wouldn't it be nice if we could blame all the world's problems on vampires? That's the trap; It's too good to be true. Hearing about vampires corrupting the government is like reading that there are horny singles in your area. Only an idiot would click on that link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-20-2020, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T02:32:54-07:00","id":1390233,"title":"","content":"We have people who believes that the earth is flat and the moon is a 2D projection. Everything is possible.<br /> <br /> Also, vampires (and other supernaturals) could have been responsible for these fake conspiracies. Filling the internet with more and more lies to deceive, distract. Like in Men in Black<br /> <br /> Try to google &quot;who's behind the power&quot; and you will find reptilians, masonry, aliens, demons, vampires, and so on. Maybe one of the tricks for keeping up the masquerade is exasperating people with more and more theories so everithing is unbelievable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T11:05:08-07:00","id":1390334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390167#post1390167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that's always puzzled me: fixable Masquerade breaches are probably inevitable and constant. So when is a Masquerade breach considered something you are presumed to be in the routine process of cleaning up, and when is it something that gets you executed while someone else cleans up your mess as you are dragged to the chopping block?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main question is, are you doing something that isn\u2019t considered normal, respectable behavior by the elite Kindred of the domain, and/or is someone in power out to get you? If neither of those is true, it makes more sense for the Prince et al. to help you fix your mistake and leave you grateful for it. Threats of final death etc, are for those whose recklessness is likely to escalate and/or those the Prince wants to be rid of anyway.<br /> <br /> I think everybody knows little slips happen from night to night, and the Camarilla establishment in a city derives a lot of its clout from being able to smooth things over. Also, if you forgive someone for screwing up, that person has learned a lesson and will think twice next time. If you kill them for it, no lesson is learned, and next time you\u2019re dealing with a fresh idiot who doesn\u2019t owe you a favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T11:05:34-07:00","id":1390336,"title":"","content":"The Masquerade I think is a bit like psychohistory in the Isaac Asimov Foundation novels. It works really well and consistently because of human nature and the fact habit and a tendency towards the status quo are a thing. And even when there are potential disruptions you may have outside elements that can address some disruptive elements. But if something really disruptive and outside your control comes along, then it all goes to hell (and probably quite fast.) And while there are always varying segments of humanity that will believe anything and have a built in desire to try to rationalize ambiguity even if the answer is wrong, there is still limits to that. <br /> <br /> So it ultimately comes down to what others said, it's going to be a headcanon/Storyteller decision that will be handled on a case by case basis because it's always a matter of degree ('how' sufficiently disruptive to break the Masquerade, and how naive/gullible the 'sheeple' are.) The setting is open ended enough to allow for both ends of the spectrum to exist reasonably well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T19:08:40-07:00","id":1390432,"title":"","content":"In my setting a group of vampires (supported somewhat by a few of the movers and shakers in the Camarilla) created a popular television drama that airs on Omnivision with with novels, movies, video games, etc., called &quot;Midnight Blood&quot; as a way to help uphold the Masquerade. Midnight Blood has a lot of similarities to the in-setting reality of the Camarilla, with different clans of vampires (some of which are pretty similar to the actual clans), a religious sect of dangerous marauding vampires, etc. It's got a really rabid fanbase, conventions, cosplay contests, a big MMO and so on. If someone were to find out about the Camarilla and the Masquerade and then try to come forward and present their findings to the masses, response from most people would be to say, &quot;What? Camarilla? You mean the Council of Fangs in Midnight Blood? Dude, that's a fantasy television show, it's not real. Stop being crazy and get help.&quot;<br /> <br /> The result would be It would be like someone in our world insisting everything in the Harry Potter books was 100% real and that there really were wizards and witches and a school for magicians in Britain. Really! People would just roll their eyes.<br /> <br /> Of course, older kindred don't really understand the &quot;hiding in plain sight&quot; concept so they view Midnight Blood as a profound Masquerade breach. And at the time it came out there was some major intra-sect conflict. At this point however it's out there, the damage is done, it's not like they can make everyone forget about the series and the Masquerade didn't explode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T19:56:05-07:00","id":1390444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390432#post1390432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The result would be It would be like someone in our world insisting everything in the Harry Potter books was 100% real and that there really were wizards and witches and a school for magicians in Britain. Really! People would just roll their eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an awesome idea! Would you mind if I were to add it to my game table?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T20:02:23-07:00","id":1390447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390432#post1390432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my setting a group of vampires (supported somewhat by a few of the movers and shakers in the Camarilla) created a popular television drama that airs on Omnivision with with novels, movies, video games, etc., called &amp;quot;Midnight Blood&amp;quot; as a way to help uphold the Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re ALMOST there... <br /> <br /> What they REALLY did to hide in plain sight was form a company called White Wolf and released a tabletop RPG called... \u201cVampire the Masquerade.\u201d<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T21:21:22-07:00","id":1390466,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s pretty much what Dracula did in the official setting. Apparently pissed some people off at time, but in the long run it seems to have worked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T21:50:46-07:00","id":1390477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390466#post1390466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s pretty much what Dracula did in the official setting. Apparently pissed some people off at time, but in the long run it seems to have worked.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my campaign, the publishing of Dracula and other vampire fiction had a number of unintended consequences for the vampire race as a whole.<br /> <br /> * The first one was the fact that it changed the way the Masquerade was enforced as now many more people knew what vampires were but they believed they were fiction and that was harder to believe when people claimed they were real.<br /> * The second one was the fact that Caitiff and Thin Bloods dramatically increased in number. 9/10 before, when a vampire was Embraced and abandoned by their sire, they died in short order because it was an impossible to understand sanity-blasting experience. The ubiquotousness of Dracula meant that these people now went, &quot;Oh, I'm a vampire.&quot; This moved it from 9/10 to like 5/10 and thus it became an actual problem.<br /> * The number of independent vampire hunters began to steadily rise. Things like the Inquisition were the only game in town but now it was possible for someone like the Frog Brothers to survive a successful hunt. Gradually, these people formed their own groups and gangs. It's been a slow burn but it has killed thousands of vampires over the years.<br /> <br /> Generally, my view on the Masquerade is the fact that it is something that is hard to DESTROY but relatively easy to INJURE. One of my book trilogies is the Red Room saga (Esoterrorism, Eldritch Ops, and The Fall of the House) which is about how a magical Illuminati-esque group keeps the supernatural secret from the public. The House is hard to stop because it controls governments, media, and has, well, magic.<br /> <br /> So various groups want to destroy it and come up with increasingly severe and horrible plans to break the Masquerade (called &quot;The Big Lie&quot;) permanently. This includes a vampire-blood based zombie plague and trying to summon a Godzilla-sized Elder God at one point. Other things can be covered up, even including the destruction of a small town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T06:41:38-07:00","id":1390542,"title":"","content":"In my eyes the Masquerade survives because the people at the top end of the various organizations that hunt vampires realize vampires for the most part adhere to secrecy. Once you make their existence public the reason for them to maintain secrecy disappears which causes a number of undesirable outcomes.<ul><li>Casualties will skyrocket. The more violent vampires will no longer hold themselves at bay instead going on killing sprees. Any important public figure will be a target (basically picture Russel Edgington's TV attack and multiply that by a large number, what he does is not beyond the capability of a young vampire in VtM).<ul><li>They have the casualty numbers among their own organizations to attest to what vampires being assailed on what are considered advantageous terms can inflict.</li> <li>Related to that is they no longer get to fight them on mostly advantageous terms. When vampires go on the offensive it means that these organizations now have to play the reactive role. There's an awful lot of people and cities to try and protect.</li> </ul></li> <li>Not everyone is going to want to attack vampires. Some will argue that they're simply suffering from a condition and try to help them. Others will want to take advantage of their capabilities.<ul><li>Vampire blood can quickly become one of the biggest tools on this particular facet of conflict.<ul><li>It halts the aging process. There are any number of wealthy, powerful, and influential people who would gladly pay and work with vampires to insure they never need worry about death's specter.</li> <li>It contains healing properties that make it better than many, if not all, the medicines we have available.<ul><li>Imagine the argument that can be made &quot;Do you have a loved one suffering from cancer? What would you give to make them better, right now? We can help you. You don't have to watch your loved ones waste away any longer. Call the Camarilla and we'll make sure your grandparents get to see their grandchildren, parents can watch their children grow up, and couples can enjoy spending their lives together. Camarilla - we're here to help.&quot;</li> <li>Modern medicine has long dealt with treatment regimens for chronic conditions. The addictive nature of vampire blood is about the only side effect of vampire blood, pretty much everything else is an upside. Just frame it as long term treatment and the pharmaceutical industry either needs to get with the blood or go out of business.</li> </ul></li> <li>From a government perspective vampires could quickly end up being treated like nuclear weapons. Whether or not you use them, you assume your foes will. Thus you have to have them or you put yourself at a tactical disadvantage.<ul><li>Essentially every Discipline has direct military application. Vampires could easily become a sort of special forces in the military, used for the toughest missions or to counter their enemies' equivalent.<ul><li>Ghouldom could become compulsory. Imagine a group of soldiers devoted to their commanding officer. They're stronger, faster, and better than a human. It wouldn't be that difficult to imagine the WoD military selecting their best officers to become vampiric commanders, not only do you never lose their battlefield experience but they make sure their troops follow orders to the letter.</li> </ul></li> <li>Even beyond legitimate political entities the idea of a rogue nation or terrorist group working with vampires could easily sway military minds into taking advantage of vampires of their own.<ul><li>You can't hope to outlive a ghoul or vampiric terrorist leader, you have to eliminate them</li> <li>Your forces are only as secure as your ability to monitor and counter Disciplines like Dominate, Presence, and Obfuscate<ul><li>Its almost impossible to consider an area clear since there could be someone with an assault rifle waiting to ambush soldiers with Obfuscate</li> </ul></li> <li>Animalism turns IEDs into guided missiles. Suddenly every stray might be a squad killing explosive<ul><li>Or they might be one of the enemy taking the guise of an animal to get into killing range</li> </ul></li> <li>Celerity makes facing them in direct combat factors more deadly. Even low level abilities like Rapid Reflexes and Blink mean a squad will probably face casualties before they can even engage</li> <li>Wards and Warding Circles make assaulting territory much harder. You never know when you're going to run into a barrier that inflicts casualties before you even close with the enemy</li> <li>There's a host of Discipline applications for the field of combat, these are just a few examples of the headaches that a commander would face fighting a vampire backed foe</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>The legal ramifications could choke the legal system for years<ul><li>Something as fundamental as &quot;is a vampire still a citizen?&quot;. Similar to the &quot;they just have a condition&quot; above there could be legal arguments that they should still hold legal rights.<ul><li>Aside from a condition they're possessed of their mental faculties and capable of making rational decisions. They could argue they should not be considered deceased, they still move and function just fine.</li> <li>Trying to argue that they lack certain functions only opens up avenues of attack<ul><li>Vampires can't have children - So sterile people and those who've had procedures that removed or damaged reproductive should lose their citizenship?</li> <li>Vampires don't eat - Blush of life from a number of vampires quickly disabuse this notion. Arguing they have trouble eating opens up assaults from the view of any number of dietary troubles</li> <li>They can't go out into the sun - So the person with serious life threatening allergies ceases to be a citizen?</li> <li>Their organs don't work - Plenty of medical conditions end up with organs not functioning properly or needing to be replaced with artificial ones, do they stop being citizens? How many prosthetic parts does it take before someone is not a citizen?</li> </ul></li> <li>In a twist of irony animal rights organizations could become their closest allies<ul><li>They literally talk to animals, you only need a few facts that only an animal might know or have experienced to eventually confirm this. How much better do their arguments become if a vampire can confirm what they say.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Many organizations and individuals will be faced with either working with the vampires or suffering<ul><li>How many corporations are going to find they have vampiric investors and shareholders through shell corporations and holdings? Suddenly every business is going to have to devote massive resources to checking every one of their records for problems.<ul><li>This only multiplies when you start looking for ghouls</li> </ul></li> <li>Many will be faced with the revelation of their darkest secrets or crimes<ul><li>This is the World of Darkness after all, we know there are corrupt criminal businessmen all over the place. To say nothing of their own personal sins</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Religious organizations are upended by proof of the supernatural<ul><li>The moment the term Cainite and the origins of vampires starts to come out non-Abrahamic faiths will have to respond. Either they need to find and adapt similar stories or face the argument that there is living magical proof that they are wrong</li> <li>A pall of doubt on any number of miracles could start to crop up as the obvious comparison to Disciplines and the powers of the blood</li> <li>The accusations and arguments over why vampires exist could divide various religious groups further. Each blaming the others sins for the existence of vampirism</li> <li>When the SI's activities become public (an active vampire foe with little to lose pretty much insures it will) there will be a lot of questions of oversight. To say nothing of concerns about authority. Just look at the worries when Kennedy was running for president that the United States president could be subservient to the Pope. Now you have evidence of a papal backed hit squad.<ul><li>Any mistakes or false targets they took out become arguments why fighting vampires is a losing proposition. If the best experts can screw up identifying a vampire versus a person, are they really that different?</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>There's the fundamental personal problem that many people will know a vampire<ul><li>There's plenty of discussion around Touchstones but it pretty much insures that a host of people will know a vampire personally. While some would abandon the vampires, others are going to stick with the friend or even more their family member</li> <li>Which leads into a big one, most people aren't going to want their family members being executed because they turn out to be vampires<ul><li>Imagine when a political figure finds out a niece, nephew, uncle, or even direct family member is a vampire. You don't think some of them are going to use all their influence to help out their family? As more and more vampires are discovered it becomes harder to claim conflict of interests and recusal.</li> </ul></li> <li>Even without vampires voting, countries with elections could find vampire friendly governments being elected. Suddenly legislation is being passed to restore their rights and figure out the legalities of their conditions. In the meantime their foes are facing down legal challenges to their activities</li> <li>Trying to accuse vampires of murder because of feeding becomes fraught with problems. The SI's actions pretty much prove the point that if they tried to seek help they would be hunted and destroyed</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> Basically vampires going public has every chance to blow up in the various hunter organizations faces, with them being portrayed as fringe religious lunatics who want to kill people's relatives because of a dietary and allergy condition. If nothing else it makes their activities much harder because they no longer have the nebulous oversight they do now, instead they'll be under a microscope from liability and litigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T09:03:36-07:00","id":1390558,"title":"","content":"Well there is that, and with the powers vampires have it's not difficult to imagine all the &quot;Do vampires deserve human rights?&quot; and &quot;Vampires are just victims&quot; stuff going their way. Maybe all the &quot;political correctness&quot; of the last few neoliberal decades have been gearing up for vampires. Maybe they'll get called <i>mortally challenged. </i> Maybe the news cycle will constantly be guilt tripping the world on all the racism/genocides/wrong side of history stuff the world's had in the past century.<br /> <br /> There are two outcomes to the masquerade shattering.<br /> A: Peace and understanding (And the vampires probably get special rights of privacy to hide from all the nazi-types that wanna burn them; A masquerade of &quot;we're nice and friendly vampires&quot; ensues. <br /> B: Apocalyptic war.<br /> <br /> or some mixture thereof.<br /> <br /> But I think, ultimately the primary stopper for the masquerade break is the actual process of a masqurade breach<br /> <br /> Inciting event occurs&gt;No vampire intervention&gt;Witness must correctly identify the attack as vampiric and not rationalize it as something else&gt; Witness must decide to take action despite consequences-<br /> <br /> A- Witness goes after the vampire themselves. Not a problem.<br /> B- Witness decides to tell the <b>media</b>&gt;Reporter must believe the story&gt; Reporter must decide to take the story further despite consequences&gt;Editor must believe the story&gt; editor must decide to take the story further despite consequences&gt; No vampire intervention&gt; Media outlet must reach a wide base of people&gt; public have to believe the story&gt;story has to spread unopposed.<br /> C- Witness tells <b>police</b>&gt; Beat cop must not die of laughter&gt; Beat cop gets homicide specialists/forensics involved&gt; nobody is influenced by vampires, vampires do not intervene&gt; murder specialists do not rationalize situtation and agree with the vampire cause&gt; Vampires do not intervene&gt; Superiors do not intervene&gt; police allow the media to get involved. <b>See B</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Now, despite the camarilla using &quot;The Masquerade&quot; as an excuse for the prince to exercise power and gain favour, the organization does still care about the masquerade and emphasizing the masquerade to bring neonates to heel is important. Getting people to practice plugging minor breeches that would otherwise fizzle out is important. Just having the vampire populace on their toes is enough.<br /> <br /> Most player characters are morons because they are controlled by players are playing a game. The setting is usually a city during turbulent times, because the players are playing a game. But most cities aren't going through great turbulence, most characters aren't controlled by PCs (or are written like Storyteller PCs, though those are plentiful). Most characters adapt to undead life and aren't a walking comedy of errors,Most cities are slow burning; Plans that last centuries, political rivals already defeated, surrounded by cities of the same sect, city comfortably corrupt. There's little Masquerade risk. On the otherhand the places where <i>shit's going down</i> and the pc's are going wild a masquerade breach needs to compete with all the noise of the usual crime waves and bankruptcies that ensue during such times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-21-2020, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T10:23:42-07:00","id":1390573,"title":"","content":"My personal take is that London and Montreal were DEFCON-1 situations. The exception, rather than the norm. London was the result of a group of in-the-know humans watching, learning, and planning for years, while the Kindred scoffed at the occasional losses and disappearances as random, unconnected incidents. Montreal happened because it was the Sabbat Vatican, how could Montreal <i>not</i> suffer a &gt;90% Cainite population loss? The Sabbat never took humanity as a serious threat, the Camarilla thought they could be clever and turn the SI into a weapon. The purge of London and Montreal will forever be warnings to the rest of Kindred society... until Kindred get lazy and complacent again, that is. <br /> <br /> All this means is that Kindred know their shadow wars are going to have to become a lot more private and inconspicuous. No more vohzd strolling down the streets of Washington.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T10:39:12-07:00","id":1390577,"title":"","content":"I should note that my own urban fantasy <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Literature/TheUnitedStatesOfMonsters\" target=\"_blank\">United States of Monsters</a> universe (compromising 4 trilogies so far) is set in a Post-Masquerade Breach world. I've devoted a lot of words and ideas to following up the concepts of how ancient rivalries (shifters and vampires, demons and humans, wizards and fairies) are settled now that they are subject to human law. Weirdly, my opinion for my own books is closer to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a>'s view of the Masquerade versus how I treat it for the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> In the WOD, especially 5th Edition, it's a death sentence to Kindred.<br /> <br /> While in my world, I do have money make the vampires the most privileged and &quot;model&quot; minority of the supernaturals despite objectively being the WORST.<br /> <br /> Why? Because money and looks trump the fact shifters are objectively less harmful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390573#post1390573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal take is that London and Montreal were DEFCON-1 situations. The exception, rather than the norm. London was the result of a group of in-the-know humans watching, learning, and planning for years, while the Kindred scoffed at the occasional losses and disappearances as random, unconnected incidents. Montreal happened because it was the Sabbat Vatican, how could Montreal <i>not</i> suffer a &gt;90% Cainite population loss? The Sabbat never took humanity as a serious threat, the Camarilla thought they could be clever and turn the SI into a weapon. The purge of London and Montreal will forever be warnings to the rest of Kindred society... until Kindred get lazy and complacent again, that is.<br /> <br /> All this means is that Kindred know their shadow wars are going to have to become a lot more private and inconspicuous. No more vohzd strolling down the streets of Washington.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I have mixed feelings about the purge of London because it's flat out been retconned. A lot of people have come up with elaborate conspiracy theories about how Schrekt or Tremere was responsible for the Fall of Vienna.<br /> <br /> That's just straight up true about London now. Mithras is the reason the government gave Project: Antigen almost unlimited authority because his cult has been the secret masters of the British Isles since Diocletian. They had all the money, weapons, and support they needed plus a near complete listing of every Kindred in the city as well as their Elysiums.<br /> <br /> It's like asking how Catwoman broke into the world's most secure vault only to find out that the owner left it open and the turned off the security system.<br /> <br /> Is it more believable? Well, fuck yes, but it pretty much defeats the purpose of the Second Inquisition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-21-2020, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T14:56:31-07:00","id":1390630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last#post1390032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Unless thermal imaging devices become extroadinarily common place...</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20200521005446/en/Global-Medical-Thermometers-Market-Trajectory-Analytics-2020-2025\" target=\"_blank\">You're right. The Masquerade will hold until there is widespread thermal screening. Phyew. The Kindred must be relieved to know they're safe. </a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T17:55:06-07:00","id":1390670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390577#post1390577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it more believable? Well, fuck yes, but it pretty much defeats the purpose of the Second Inquisition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but take consolation in the fact that the SI slipped from his control, even before he met final death. The first Inquisition (FI?) started because of kindred politics, and slipped out of their control, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T19:41:48-07:00","id":1390685,"title":"","content":"What people don't understand about the masquerade is that it's not really a necessity, but a convinience. Think about it, if vampires suddenly decided to come out in the open, then they'll have to start obeying human laws. What happens when you accidentaly drain a vessel, or go into frenzy and kill a bunch of humans? For vampires this is natural behavior, an inevitable part of being a cainite, but to humans this is murder and it needs to be punished.<br /> <br /> How about ghouling and blood bonding? Is it legal to drug someone into loving you? Into having sexual relations with you? To make them a into a slave for the rest of their (supernaturally extended) life? Of course not, the courts would throw the book at you! But again, for vampires this is just a part of being kindred.<br /> <br /> So you see, vampires and humans are really not the same, nor are they equals. The societies they build also have to be very different, because if the Camarilla decided to, for example, make killing humans a punishable offense, pretty much every vampire would have to be punished.<br /> <br /> Vampires and humans are totally incompatable, and frankly, living openly alongside humans in an equitable fashion would be a real drag for the average bloodsucking monster that can tank bullets and kill people in a single blow. That's the real reason the masquerade exists. Because the alternative is either enslave the humans openly, which is an entierly superfluous option to any camarilla ancilla and upward, or be enslaved by them and have to follow their laws, their customs ect. Just a waste of time either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T21:37:19-07:00","id":1390699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390630#post1390630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20200521005446/en/Global-Medical-Thermometers-Market-Trajectory-Analytics-2020-2025\" target=\"_blank\">You're right. The Masquerade will hold until there is widespread thermal screening. Phyew. The Kindred must be relieved to know they're safe. </a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, eventually they're going to have to come out with an edition where vampires are simply harder to detect. Vampires being cold will have to join not casting a reflection in the myth department. Which shouldn't be difficult. I mean, how many movies even use that trope? By the 6th or 7th edition, if people are still playing this game, they will have to drop the need for using blood to raise your temperature, because that weakness will become too fatal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T21:39:20-07:00","id":1390700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390699#post1390699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, eventually they're going to have to come out with an edition where vampires are simply harder to detect. Vampires being cold will have to join not casting a reflection in the myth department. Which shouldn't be difficult. I mean, how many movies even use that trope? By the 6th or 7th edition, if people are still playing this game, they will have to drop the need for using blood to raise your temperature, because that weakness will become too fatal.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can say the Blood Thickened to be warm so only vampires completely without blood are able to be detected via thermal scan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T21:52:26-07:00","id":1390702,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* Regardless, vampires being cold is something rarely used in movies anymore, possibly because it's too obvious a giveaway if a protagonist shakes the vampire's hand and it is icy cold. &quot;Fright Night&quot; would have been over the moment Jerry shook hands with anyone, especially in the scene where Peter Vincent, Amy, and Ed come over and he is shaking everyone's hands and kissing Amy's hand. Irrc, the Langella Dracula would have had a similar problem. Most modern fiction tends to go with the idea that vampire's appear completely human until some provocation causes them to drop their mask. Basically, fictional vampires have a human appearance and temperature as their default, and only lose them when they fail the equivalent of a self-control or Composure+Resolve roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T21:53:21-07:00","id":1390703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390702#post1390702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs* Regardless, vampires being cold is something rarely used in movies anymore, possibly because it's too obvious a giveaway if a protagonist shakes the vampire's hand and it is icy cold. &quot;Fright Night&quot; would have been over the moment Jerry shook hands with anyone, especially in the scene where Peter Vincent, Amy, and Ed come over and he is shaking everyone's hands and kissing Amy's hand. Irrc, the Langella Dracula would have had a similar problem. Most modern fiction tends to go with the idea that vampire's appear completely human until some provocation causes them to drop their mask. Basically, fictional vampires have a human appearance and temperature as their default, and only lose them when they fail the equivalent of a self-control or Composure+Resolve roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, vampires are room temperature. That's different from ice cold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T00:50:36-07:00","id":1390722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390630#post1390630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20200521005446/en/Global-Medical-Thermometers-Market-Trajectory-Analytics-2020-2025\" target=\"_blank\">You're right. The Masquerade will hold until there is widespread thermal screening. Phyew. The Kindred must be relieved to know they're safe. </a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vampires are room teperature. They're not the cold corpses of certain fiction. <br /> <br /> <br /> 1- These are short range devices brought out during peak times? (during the day) right? (I could be wrong). I think most vampires would be able to weasel themselves out of a short range test through dominate/animalism/obfuscate/thaumaturgy. In a long sweep of a crowd, i think it's likely the vampire'd get lost in the scan. people are looking for those too hot, being too cold is an oddity, but not something that needs following up. People are looking for positives, not unusually strong negatives. <br /> <br /> 2. I've thought about this. If blush of life is too inconvenient: <br /> 1- A thaumaturgy ritual. There's a level 1 ritual involving a blood vial that lets you mimick a human function, and a more specialized ritual would be in development during this time. <br /> 2- Heating devices on your person<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I haven't seen one of these devices yet. I think kindred can organize and warn eachother of areas where they're put up using their contacts in the goverment, and they can have these devices quietly removed when the panic subsides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T01:15:47-07:00","id":1390726,"title":"","content":"A room temperature person feels really cold. Ever have your wife put her cold feet on you in bed? That is pretty cold and it\u2019s warmer than room temperature. I\u2019m not saying that shaking hands with someone with really cold hands is going to instantly make you think of a vampire, but it will seem a bit weird. A thermal imaging device that can detect a person a few degrees warmer than normal should have no trouble detecting a vampire that is room temperature. though that is an easy fix, just rule that vampires are warm.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I can\u2019t really get into the idea of broken Masquerade settings. They always seem too normal, too much the real world. A setting in which vampires are openly revealed to the public isn\u2019t going to be like the real 2020 with vampires as a discriminated against minority group. The world that results from that sort of revelation is going to be a science fiction or fantasy setting. Either vampires will be ruthlessly purged or society will revolve around them. There can\u2019t be an in between with creatures that can control minds or grant immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T01:36:34-07:00","id":1390728,"title":"","content":"At night time, it's often normal for someone's body surface to feel cold. Depends where you are. But I think it's something vampires can work around given awareness. They have the contacts and information networks to be informed, assuming they share this information in elysium, which, despite being vampires, I'd assume they would for &quot;the greater good&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T06:54:57-07:00","id":1390763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390699#post1390699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, eventually they're going to have to come out with an edition where vampires are simply harder to detect. Vampires being cold will have to join not casting a reflection in the myth department.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would prefer it to be something covered by &quot;blush of life.&quot; With &quot;blush of life&quot; it is not an automatic thing, meaning the PCs have to remember to use it and so can trip up or otherwise make a mistake. Simply having it as an automatic thing (i.e. vampires are warm as a living person) would be giving them, the PCs, an automatic success. And thematically keeping vampires warm would be a compromise as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T06:59:00-07:00","id":1390764,"title":"","content":"The Blush of Life does affect this already, and in the current edition it can last all night. In the last game I ran, hunters did make use of thermal imaging, but they didn\u2019t understand the Blush of Life, so the PCs were still able to trick them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T07:05:31-07:00","id":1390765,"title":"","content":"This probably deserves an article but I always felt that the Masquerade needed a chart that would describe, &quot;How well is the Masquerade holding in any given area?&quot; Because the Masquerade is not really something that is useful to a game if it can be shattered by one cellphone but also saying, &quot;It's immune to breaking&quot; isn't worthwhile either.<br /> <br /> Also, there's a lot of stuff that can screw with a vampire's life before it hits &quot;People know vampires exist.&quot;<br /> <br /> Example: A Thin Blooded serial killer is operating in Chicago's Rack, tracking down women and draining them dry in a way that has gotten on the news and tabloids despite the best efforts of vampires to contain it. No one thinks it's REALLY a vampire. Don't be stupid. However, they do think there's a guy who THINKS he's a vampire murdering people around town. This makes things INCREDIBLY difficult for the Kindred of Chicago.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, there's people protesting outside of the Succubus Club and Red 9. Women are staying home and avoiding clubbing because of the existence of said serial killer. Parents are watching their teens and trying to get them not to go clubbing or to leave the Goth scene where feeding was once very able. The police are also investigating all of the locations where blood-drinking has been reported as a &quot;fetish&quot; over the years and interrogating ghouls, Herds, and casual witnesses. There's also the fact that those &quot;aware&quot; are now actually likely to descend on this area.<br /> <br /> The vampires CAN contain this and certainly will but it's a pain in the ass and makes operating much-much harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T07:45:03-07:00","id":1390769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390764#post1390764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Blush of Life does affect this already, and in the current edition it can last all night. In the last game I ran, hunters did make use of thermal imaging, but they didn\u2019t understand the Blush of Life, so the PCs were still able to trick them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is my point. The PCs had to make the choice, and spend the resource (the blood point) to have the blush of life. It was not an automatic thing, the rules did not do it for them. I prefer that the choice come down to the PCs. Not that it be made for the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T08:29:49-07:00","id":1390777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390769#post1390769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is my point. The PCs had to make the choice, and spend the resource (the blood point) to have the blush of life. It was not an automatic thing, the rules did not do it for them. I prefer that the choice come down to the PCs. Not that it be made for the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, you\u2019re correct: making vampires innately undetectable would deprive players of a choice, which is not a good thing for a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T08:42:22-07:00","id":1390784,"title":"","content":"The thing is, once technology reaches a certain level of ubiquitousness, it ceases to be a choice, and simply becomes you making two rouse checks each rising as a matter of necessity. At which point you might as well just say, &quot;eh, vampires appear human unless they fail Composure+Revolve rolls when under stress&quot;, to make it like &quot;Fright Night&quot; and such, where Jerry looks human until someone stabs him in the hand, or pisses him off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T09:16:53-07:00","id":1390796,"title":"","content":"Vampires can put in a lot of work to stop thermal cameras being ubiquitous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T10:33:31-07:00","id":1390806,"title":"","content":"This is a bit aside from the current thermal discussion, I don't really know enough about it to speak with authority on anything so for the time being I leave it in the realm of technologically capable hunters and the occasional clever neonate and technomancer.<br /> <br /> What I'm really interested with, fully admitting that this is the system loving side of my brain, is a sort of chart graphing the level that an area's local Masquerade is at, somewhat akin to Reality Zones from Mage or the systems described in VtR's Damnation City.<br /> <br /> I don't know, but I really do like the idea of a 1-5 or 1-10 chart of degrees which can talk about the nature of the masquerade in a certain area and how it effects the local vampiric and human population whether it's from 5 (Halls of Learning; vampires are a myth), 3 (City Streets; strange things happen, but magic probably isn't real) all the way down to 0 (Masquerade Broken). <br /> <br /> But like I said, I've got a soft spot for nice systems and charts, so this well could just be me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T13:55:22-07:00","id":1390845,"title":"","content":"Vampires can also take saunas with a meat thermometer in their mouths until they hit 98.6\u00b0F and have several hours to walk around under normal circumstances before they lose enough heat to be obviously colder than a normal person. Or sleep the day away under electric blankets, or in a hot room, etc. Thermal imaging to catch blank bodies is only going to work on the stupid or those inhuman enough not to care once it becomes known they're a thing in use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T14:03:25-07:00","id":1390847,"title":"","content":"They can also use the Blush of Life unless they're Cappadocians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T09:39:43-07:00","id":1442405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1390558#post1390558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there is that, and with the powers vampires have it's not difficult to imagine all the &quot;Do vampires deserve human rights?&quot; and &quot;Vampires are just victims&quot; stuff going their way. Maybe all the &quot;political correctness&quot; of the last few neoliberal decades have been gearing up for vampires. Maybe they'll get called <i>mortally challenged. </i> Maybe the news cycle will constantly be guilt tripping the world on all the racism/genocides/wrong side of history stuff the world's had in the past century.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually really interesting. I could see it happening, but I wouldn't go that route as a storyteller because it would alter the game way too much. It would turn it into a cross between True Blood and Anita Blake: Vampire Hunter. Take away the Masquerade, and you take away the whole point of roleplaying a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26415-cultofjimmy","name":"CultofJimmy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T09:46:35-07:00","id":1442408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CultofJimmy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1442405#post1442405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is actually really interesting. I could see it happening, but I wouldn't go that route as a storyteller because it would alter the game way too much. It would turn it into a cross between True Blood and Anita Blake: Vampire Hunter. Take away the Masquerade, and you take away the whole point of roleplaying a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a guy who has a world of public vampires and shifters, I agree. It's the difference between Urban Fantasy and Horror.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T12:28:32-07:00","id":1442421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CultofJimmy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1442405#post1442405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is actually really interesting. I could see it happening, but I wouldn't go that route as a storyteller because it would alter the game way too much. It would turn it into a cross between True Blood and Anita Blake: Vampire Hunter. Take away the Masquerade, and you take away the whole point of roleplaying a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There'd still be a masquerade, only it's a shift to a more -It's us, perfectly innocent vampires, working charities, treating the mentally ill, showing off our musical skills and imparting our knowledge of long lost history for the good of mankind. We certainly aren't doing anything bad or even mildly scandalous, anything at all, no-sir-e. Don't come in now, there's dust everywhere&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T12:47:28-07:00","id":1442425,"title":"","content":"So once vampires go public it just shifts from vampire biker gangs to vampire corporations. Vampires become the Elves in the movie Bright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T13:25:19-07:00","id":1442430,"title":"","content":"It becomes Shadowrun with vampires, basically. Which is how games in the nineties often were anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T17:26:52-07:00","id":1442446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1442425#post1442425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So once vampires go public it just shifts from vampire biker gangs to vampire corporations. Vampires become the Elves in the movie Bright.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally you can run 90% of V:TM games without changing much.<br /> <br /> It just means humans are even more stupid to let the wolves walk among the sheep.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T18:28:12-07:00","id":1442451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390032-vtm-why-the-masquerade-will-last?p=1442446#post1442446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally you can run 90% of V:TM games without changing much.</div> </div> </div> </div>The few times I messed with it, the short term is as you say about 90% the same. But once you allow some time to pass, the small adjustments you have to make have larger setting ramifications.<br /> <br /> A good example is that the Masquerade shifted from restricting information about vampires to purging vampires who weren't on morality Paths that were compatible with being public. Also because humans are a fickle bunch, the less human the clan or bloodline appeared, the more they were suppressed.<br /> <br /> One of the more interesting turn arounds is the Salubri, since they have one of the more humane discipline combos and their weakness is practically good PR for humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}